# ============================================================================
# llvm_shim.vel -- the Vela side of the compiler's own code generator.
#
# GENERATED by tools\gen-shim-decls.ps1 from runtime\vela_llvm_shim.h.
# Do not edit by hand: edit the header and regenerate, or the two sides drift
# and the failure surfaces as an undefined symbol in a file nobody touched.
#
# This is the bridge that makes the north star reachable: `vm.exe` carries
# libLLVM inside it (through these calls) instead of shelling out to a C
# compiler, so `vm.exe build x.vel` can write an object file itself and leave
# only the executable in the user's directory.
#
# The C types map by the compiler's own rule (emit_ctype, emit.vel:177):
# int64_t -> int, int32_t -> i32, uint8_t -> u8, double -> float,
# bool -> bool, vela_str -> str, void -> None.
#
# 75 declarations, in the header's order.
# ============================================================================

# Handles (modules, types, functions, blocks, values) are `int` here because
# they are opaque pointers in C: the emitter passes them back unchanged and
# never looks inside one.

